{
  "reasons": {
    "other-verse-2-20": "LXX2012's English here renders Greek of the verse before or after, which has no English chunk of its own to point at, so a chunk cannot point at it (the like of Genesis 37:32): Isaiah 3:8's last clause is 3:9's first, and 3:9 and 3:10 hold the English of the Greek verses 3:9 and 3:10 in turn; 3:17's 'in that day' is the Greek of 3:18; the English of 3:21 to 3:24 is that of the Greek 3:20 to 3:26 (ear-rings, scarlet, sweet smell, sword, stores), whose words sit in other verses; 6:8 ends with the English of the Greek 6:9 (Go, and say to this people); 13:21 ends with the English of the Greek 13:22 (hedgehogs, nests, satyrs); 18:3 begins with the English of the end of the Greek 18:2 ('the rivers of the land') (mw-u2w5klk.349.14).",
    "added-2-20": "Either Brenton adds it to make English of a Greek phrase ('reason' of 'by reason of', 'order' of 'in order to', 'forth' of 'go forth', 'aside', 'become', 'own', 'only', 'anything', 'back', 'away', 'together', 'soon') or the Greek word that renders it is a pair the aligner made to another English word that the model pass does not move (the Greek of 'camp' of 8:8, 'deserted' of 6:11, 'rise up' and the like), each read against its verse (mw-u2w5klk.349.14)."
  },
